---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "../../data/profile";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and analytics | Eero Siivola"
  description="How analytics consent and privacy choices are handled on Eero Siivola's website."
>
  <header class="evidence-hero">
    <div class="shell evidence-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy and analytics.</h1>
      </div>
      <p>
        This page describes the limited information this professional website stores and how
        optional analytics consent works.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section narrative-section">
    <div class="shell prose privacy-copy">
      <h2>Current data collection</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no accounts, contact forms, advertising, or personalised marketing. Google
        Analytics is configured with measurement ID <code>G-RK8VRLQ1ND</code>, but its tag does not
        load until you explicitly allow analytics.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics is used to understand aggregate site traffic and which pages are useful.
        Its default measurement can include session statistics, approximate location, and browser
        and device information. The Google tag is blocked unless you select
        <strong>Allow analytics</strong>. Selecting <strong>Decline analytics</strong> prevents it
        from loading and sends no consent or measurement request to Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        Advertising storage, advertising user data, and advertising personalisation remain denied
        in both cases. Google describes its handling of information in the{" "}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your saved choice</h2>
      <p>
        The site stores your analytics choice in your browser's local storage under
        <code>eero-analytics-consent-v1</code>. This strictly necessary value records only
        <code>granted</code> or <code>denied</code>. It is not sent to Eero or to Google.
      </p>
      <button class="privacy-settings-button" type="button" data-open-analytics-settings hidden>
        Change analytics settings
      </button>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Links to LinkedIn, GitHub, Google Scholar, ORCID, Vuono Group, and publication services
        take you to those organisations' websites. Their own privacy practices apply after you
        follow a link.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this site's privacy implementation can be sent through{" "}
        <a href={profile.social.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-copy h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 2.5vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .privacy-copy h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .privacy-copy code {
    padding: 0.12rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .privacy-settings-button {
    min-height: 46px;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: transparent;
    font-weight: 750;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .privacy-settings-button:hover {
    color: var(--paper);
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .privacy-settings-button[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
